        <p style="margin:0 0 10px 0; text-align:justify;">
            b. MONETARY RECOVERY TO THE CLIENT:
            If the case settles for non-monetary relief, such as a loan modification, or credit repair, client does not owe the attorney any 
            percent of the value of such a recovery.  However, if money is awarded to Client, or if money is recovered for client, 
            Attorney shall receive 33% of the gross amount of any such money.  If a lawsuit is progressing and has gone past the point 
            of the first mandatory settlement conference then 40% of the gross amount of any monetary settlement or recovery shall be the contingency amount due to the greater amount of work required.  
            Any settlement or award shall first be deposited to Attorney Client IOLTA Trust Account and then disbursed to Client.  In the event that attorney’s fees are obtained as part of a settlement, a judgment, or by court order, 
            such shall be payable to Attorney and the Firm shall keep all attorney’s fees earned.
            </p>
