<div style="margin-left:20px;">
    <div style="margin-top:-10px; padding:10px 15px; background-color:#FFFFFF; border-radius:0 8px 8px 0;">
        <p style="margin:0 0 10px 0; text-align:justify;">
           a. STANDARD COSTS:
           The following are typical costs incurred in most litigations:  Filing Fees for filing a lawsuit in Superior 
           Court -- $435.00.  Service of the lawsuit on an in state Defendant -- $75.00.  Service of the lawsuit out of 
           state -- $150.00.  Filing a Lis Pendens (which is a cloud on title filed at the County Recorders office -- $100.00). Unlawful 
           Detainer answers are approximately $300.00 per occupant. A client should expect to pay between $550 and $1,000.00 in filing 
           fees to commence the lawsuit.  Later, if client continues toward trial other costs may be necessary to put on a good trial, 
           such as deposition expenses and expert witnesses fees.  The majority of cases do not proceed so far towards trial that depositions 
           and expert witness fees are necessary, but if trial becomes necessary these fees can be high.  A deposition could cost approximately 
           $2,000.00.  Retaining experts for trial is even more costly.
         </p>
    </div>
</div>
<div style="margin-left:20px;">
    <div style="margin-top:-10px; padding:10px 15px; background-color:#FFFFFF; border-radius:0 8px 8px 0;">
        <p style="margin:0 0 10px 0; text-align:justify;">
           b. COSTS ON DISMISSAL:  
          Client further understands that should Judgment be rendered against Client at the trial of this action, or 
          Client’s claim fails the Client may be responsible to pay any costs which the Court may award to the opposing 
          party or parties, including their attorney fees.<u>This does pose a risk</u> as an attorney fee award may be imposed 
          against you.  Usually this outcome can be avoided by voluntary dismissal if the action starts doing poorly, 
          but it is a possibility if the action suddenly fails.
         </p>
    </div>
</div>

 <div style="margin-top:-10px; padding:10px 15px; background-color:#FFFFFF; border-radius:0 8px 8px 0;">
