            8. TAX DISCLOSURE AND ACKNOWLEDGMENT:    
       CLIENT IS ADVISED TO OBTAIN INDEPENDENT AND COMPETENT TAX ADVICE regarding potential settlements which may alter the 
       terms of Client’s secured debt and awards of damages in civil litigation which may have significant tax consequences.  
       The Firm does not employ tax attorneys nor offer tax advice.  Before Client consents to any settlement or award of 
       damages, Client may wish to consult a tax professional. The Firm is not responsible for any tax liability Client might 
       incur as a result of its obtaining settlements which alter the terms of Client’s secured debt, awards of damages in civil 
       litigation, or a recovery of money damages on Client’s behalf.
        </p>
    </div>
    
     <div style="margin-top:-10px; padding:10px 15px; background-color:#FFFFFF; border-radius:0 8px 8px 0;">
        <p style="margin:0 0 10px 0;text-align:justify;">
           9. ARBITRATION OF DISPUTES:       
       The parties elect herein that any fee disputes be resolved pursuant to the fee arbitration procedures of the State 
       Bar of California, in any dispute subject to the jurisdiction of the State of California over attorney's fees, 
       charges, costs or expenses, as set forth in California Business and Professions Code § 6200, et seq.  If, after 
       receiving a notice of this right to arbitrate, you do not elect to proceed under the State Bar fee arbitration 
       procedures, and do not file a request for fee arbitration within 30 days, any dispute over fees, charges, costs or 
       expenses, will be resolved by binding arbitration.
        </p>
        
       <p style="margin:0 0 10px 0;text-align:justify;">     
